<urn:atm:triage:finding/AJ-FINAL-006-GRAFT-INGRESS-UNGUARDED>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AJ-FINAL-006-GRAFT-INGRESS-UNGUARDED" ;
  triage:title "Graft's ActivityObservation ingress leg is invisible to the AJ.7 source-use guard" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-graft-python/src/lib.rs genuinely constructs and attaches ActivityObservation data via atm_core::caller_context::activity_observation_for_resolved_caller and WriteRequest/ReadQuery::with_activity_observation (lines ~370, 406-409), making it the third leg of the documented closed ingress set alongside heartbeat and CLI send/read/ack. It never spells the 3 guarded PascalCase tokens, so it has no required_positive entry in .just/lint-config.toml and is not even listed in allowed_paths -- the guard does not verify graft's wiring at all, unlike the CLI paths which each have a required_positive proving correct attachment. Found by ruthless-boundary-qa (RBQA-F001) during Phase AJ's final holistic gate review. QA source: PR #759." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AJ" ;
  triage:triageMode "phase_end_gate" ;
